- **`promisify`**: wraps a Node-style callback function (`(...args, (error, data) => ...)`) and returns a function that returns a `Promise`, rejecting on a truthy `error` and resolving with `data` otherwise.
- **`all`**: collects results by index and resolves once every promise has resolved; rejects on the first rejection. An empty array resolves immediately with `[]`.
- **`allSettled`**: waits for every promise and records `{ status, value }` or `{ status, reason }` for each, in input order.
- **`race`**: settles with whichever promise settles first.
- **`any`**: resolves with the first fulfilled value; if all reject, rejects with an `AggregateError` containing the reasons.

Each implementation uses only the `Promise` constructor and `.then`, not the static `Promise.all`, `allSettled`, `race`, or `any`. Inputs are wrapped with `new Promise(resolve => resolve(p))` so plain values are accepted too.

