- **`LinkedList`** keeps a head reference and a length counter so `__len__` is O(1). `push()` prepends, which makes the head the most recently pushed item. `__iter__` walks from the head. `reversed()` builds a new list by pushing the values in head-first order, which places the original tail at the head of the new list.
