The skeleton functions all throw, so each one needs an implementation. `promisify` wraps a callback-style function in a `Promise`. The four combinators are rebuilt with `new Promise` and each input's `.then`, without calling `Promise.all`, `Promise.allSettled`, `Promise.race`, or `Promise.any`.

- **`promisify`**: returns a wrapper that passes a Node-style callback as the last argument and resolves or rejects based on its `error` parameter. It preserves `this` and forwards all arguments.
- **`all`**: stores each result at its input index and resolves once every promise has fulfilled. The first rejection rejects the whole result. An empty array resolves to `[]`.
- **`allSettled`**: never rejects. Each slot receives `{ status, value }` or `{ status, reason }`, and the result resolves once all inputs have settled.
- **`race`**: settles with the first promise to settle, matching native behavior. An empty array never settles.
- **`any`**: resolves with the first fulfillment. If every input rejects, it rejects with an `AggregateError` holding all the reasons. An empty array rejects immediately with an empty `AggregateError`.

Each function uses `Array.from` so it accepts any iterable and wraps non-promise values with `Promise.resolve`.

