- Build an adjacency map from pip value to domino indices. A self-domino such as `[2|2]` is counted twice, which is correct.
- Reject the input if any pip value has an odd count. Such a chain can never close.
- Run Hierholzer's algorithm from the first domino's left value. Each popped vertex/edge pair gives the next domino in the circuit.
- Reject the input if the circuit doesn't use every domino, which means the dominoes are disconnected.
- Orient each domino so its left half matches the previous right half, reversing it with a helper when needed.

